# Normalise line endings so a clone on any platform behaves the same.
#
# Deliberately NOT `* text=auto`: the repository already contains mixed files,
# and a blanket rule would make git want to renormalise everything on the next
# commit — a huge, meaningless diff. Only the cases that actually matter are
# declared here.

# The build pipeline is a set of bash scripts. CRLF would break them (a
# trailing \r turns `then` into `then\r`), so they must stay LF everywhere.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never diff, never convert.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.rpk   binary
*.zip   binary
*.pem   binary
*.key   binary
